9. Compacted and Loose Thickness

Create a THICKNESS & COMPACTION section.

Fields:

- Target Compacted Thickness (mm).
- Recommended Loose Thickness (mm).
- Actual Loose Thickness (mm).
- Achieved Compacted Thickness (mm).
- Thickness Variation (mm).
- Material Density, where applicable.

Calculate loose thickness using an approved loose-to-compacted factor from:

- Approved method statement.
- Trial-section results.
- Material-specific specifications.
- JMF, where applicable.
- Verified site calibration.

Formula:

Loose Thickness = Target Compacted Thickness × Approved Loose-to-Compacted Factor.

Do not apply a universal multiplier.

If no verified factor is available, display:

Trial Section / Engineer Verification Required

Allow manual input with a clear manual-entry status.

Compare actual and target thickness only against verified project tolerances.

